          {
            "kind": "heading",
            "id": "title",
            "text": "Help",
            "level": 1
          },
          {
            "kind": "heading",
            "id": "h1",
            "text": "Installing a package",
            "level": 2
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "id": "p1",
            "text": "Run pip install followed by the project name. pip resolves the latest release compatible with your Python version, downloads the wheel or source distribution, verifies its hash and installs it into the active environment. Use a virtual environment so projects do not share dependencies."
          },
          {
            "kind": "heading",
            "id": "h2",
            "text": "Publishing a package",
            "level": 2
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "id": "p2",
            "text": "Build a wheel and a source distribution with a PEP 517 build backend, then upload with twine or a trusted publisher from CI. Releases are immutable once uploaded; a mistaken release can be yanked, which hides it from resolvers that have not pinned it, but not deleted."
          },
          {
            "kind": "heading",
            "id": "h3",
            "text": "Project names",
            "level": 2
          },
          {
            "kind": "heading",
            "id": "h4",
            "text": "Classifiers",
            "level": 2
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "id": "p4",
            "text": "Trove classifiers describe a project's status, supported Python versions and topic. They come from a fixed list; an unknown classifier is rejected at upload."
          },
          {
            "kind": "heading",
            "id": "h5",
            "text": "Getting help",
            "level": 2
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "id": "p5",
            "text": "Packaging questions belong on the Python discussion forum or on Stack Overflow under the pip and python-packaging tags. Problems with a specific project go to that project's issue tracker, linked from its page."
          },
          {
            "kind": "link",
            "id": "so",
            "text": "Packaging questions on Stack Overflow",
            "url": "http://stackoverflow.com/"
          }
        ]
      },
