            "kind": "text",
            "id": "desc",
            "text": "pyjsonlite dumps a value with keys sorted, floats in shortest round-trip form, and no insignificant whitespace, so that two processes on two platforms produce the same bytes and a hash of the output is meaningful. loads() is the standard library's. There is a diff() that returns RFC 6902 operations."
