            "id": "summary",
            "text": "A transparent on-disk cache for HTTP GET requests, keyed by URL and headers, with a deterministic replay mode."
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "id": "meta",
            "text": "License: MIT · Author: Hanna Brandt · Requires: Python >=3.9 · Latest release: 1.0.2 (2026)"
          },
          {
            "kind": "heading",
            "id": "desc-h",
            "text": "Project description",
            "level": 2
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "id": "desc",
            "text": "requests-cache-lite records every GET response to a directory and serves it back on the next call. In replay mode a request that was not recorded raises instead of going to the network, which makes a test suite hermetic. Cache keys are canonical JSON of the method, URL and selected headers, via pyjsonlite. Works with tinyhttp and with the standard library."
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "id": "rh",
            "text": "Release history: 1.0.2 (latest), 1.0.1, 1.0.0, 0.9.0"
